Tensor-parallel workers: the output thread would read each step's tokens back as soon as
the step is enqueued, and under CC that blocking readback stalls the rank's launches (and,
through the all-reduce, every rank). VLLM_CC_WORKER_DRAIN_LAG=1 holds outputs back by
depth-1 steps; VLLM_CC_WORKER_DRAIN_FLUSH_MS bounds the delay when the engine goes idle.

--- a/v1/executor/multiproc_executor.py
+++ b/v1/executor/multiproc_executor.py
